Accelerated compositing uses the upstream DMA-BUF renderer: the web process
renders with GL/Skia into GBM buffers exported as dma-buf (PRIME) fds, and
the UI process imports them as EGLImages. PRIME export/import, dma_resv and
sync_file all exist in our drm(4); what is missing is mmap(2)/ioctl(2) on
dma-buf fds (linux/dma-buf.h) and poll(2)/kqueue(2) on sync_file fds.

Do not use explicit sync (exported sync_file fences) on OpenBSD. drm(4) can
export a syncobj as a sync_file fd (EGL_ANDROID_native_fence_sync works), but
syncfile_kqfilter() returns EINVAL and DTYPE_SYNC fds have no poll handler,
so poll(2) yields POLLNVAL immediately and the UI process FenceMonitor would
consider every frame complete before the GPU finished rendering it. Wait
client-side with GLFence::clientWait() instead.

Runtime knobs for testing:
WEBKIT_DMABUF_RENDERER_FORCE_SHM=1
WEBKIT_DISABLE_DMABUF_RENDERER=1
WEBKIT_DISABLE_COMPOSITING_MODE=1

